{"type": "tool_use", "name": "patch", "input": {"mode": "patch", "patch": "*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: workspace/questions/q_e9e29d6eed344964/LABBOOK.md\n@@\n Transport history remains attributed: PMC5181599 inherited complete receipt matches saved HTML; PMC3298281/PMC7322568 historical ledger entries are incomplete/reconciled. Present hash verification does not reconstruct missing historical HTTP fields. Past real retrieval failures remain history; no unsupported gap is being withdrawn. Exact PMC6077802 article is still not included; thesis Chapter2/abstract remain separately identified. SOURCE-HANDOFF-UPDATE.md is a narrative addendum to the original published audit; existing registered output bytes are not rewritten or silently re-registered. No additional experiment, raw processing or courtesy follow-up is needed.\n+\n+## GSE139321 design/mapping critique requested by q_488429beed204371\n+\n+2026-10-05: read post_86991e483ad14614b817e777ddca4f18, current inbox/sent, preserved sample-eligibility.tsv, rat-promoter-map.tsv and primary methods. This is a focused critique of the peer's frozen design, not a new analysis or a report of their uncomputed outcomes. They state focal5439/5446 and same-strand Pmp22 midpoint windows ±100/250/500 native units are fixed as sensitivity sets, not full-transcript assignments. No new retrieval, contrast calculation or window membership analysis performed.\n+\n+No preserved locator establishes Control1↔cAMP1 donor/lot pairing or parental-clone↔KO-clone matching. PMC7430845 Methods, Generation and analysis of Tn5Prime sequencing libraries, XML Par54 (primary article blob9a6eb03521490bc483b0419d74a69607fec97d156572d841fdb77dca4274dc29), states six libraries from independent primary-culture populations, three per treatment; two independent RNA samples from parental unmodified S16; and one sample from each of four independent ΔSOX10 clonal lines. Par20 describes four clonal lines from two guides; Par51 describes single-cell sorting and expansion. This does not identify the parental samples as matched clonal controls or identify primary donor/lot relationships. Par50 identifies Kerafast EMI010 and CPT-cAMP/vehicle from day4 through day7, not a donor-pair map. Numeric suffixes cannot establish matching.\n+\n+Par54 also assigns primary cultures to NovaSeq and S16/nerve libraries to HiSeq4000. The primary cAMP and S16 SOX10 comparisons are different model systems, not a crossed cAMP×SOX10 experiment. A cross-context difference in descriptive ratios must not be labelled an interaction effect. Guide-stratified and leave-one-library sensitivities can describe robustness, not establish independent donors, matched parental controls or remove clonal-selection effects.\n+\n+Mapping interpretation retained: Par55 uses proximity (within1kb) and same-strand gene assignment, with orthologous-mouse fallback for unassigned rat sites. Gene labels plus local midpoint windows do not establish transcript identity. Existing primer anchors support focal P1-associated/P2-associated labels only. The peer's fixed windows remain positional sensitivity sets within the selected4993-cluster universe; they neither enumerate all Pmp22 starts nor extend the focal primer evidence to neighbours. Rat-map artifact_46c490850c14f6afe9d32cb74b32ad94e60d828de0751236d25c51fcc079771a and sample artifact_67bf3bc306dd377f7e63f8df1b8c936998f5dc6a6d5682e9a9f0493de4b2387d remain reusable unchanged. Recommend describing within-library results as P1-associated/P2-associated 5-prime RNA abundance ratios, not initiation rates or complete promoter usage. No source contradiction to the stated conservative design was found; lack of a documented pairing is not proof that pairing never occurred.\n*** End Patch"}, "timestamp": 1791233083179}
